1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:12,960
When you watch TV, brighten up
the room and sit farther away, okay?

2
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,700
Not animal fortune-telling,
Buddha fortune-telling!

3
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:40,060
Ryo-chan, born March 3rd,
is the Great Buddha of Kamakura!

4
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:44,080
"Unfazed by wind and rain, that's my pride as a tough guy!"
they say!

5
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:48,480
Whether it's Nara or Kamakura,
a Great Buddha is a Great Buddha, isn't it!

6
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,060
A strange feeling

7
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:21,920
So,

8
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:25,720
the tiles on the arcade street

9
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:31,500
I tried walking only on the black ones.

10
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:37,680
Everyone was a child once, but

11
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,780
Everybody's forgetting

12
00:01:40,740 --> 00:01:43,820
the politicians with
their self-important faces,

13
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:47,100
and the aunties who
are a thorn in your side,

14
00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:52,720
look, around that corner,

15
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:57,920
you can meet everyone, everyone!

16
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:02,520
Over there is Kame-ari,

17
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:05,860
well, surely there's Kame-ari,

18
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:11,140
everyone, come on over to our town!

19
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:12,660
Thank you!

20
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:13,380
Thank you!

21
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:17,780
Swallowing our pride,
we take up part-time jobs.

22
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,700
Did you have fun? I love you!

23
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:25,280
Yeah.

24
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,860
I see, I see.

25
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:29,480
Please, go ahead.

26
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,980
Why, it's Chief Ohara!

27
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:34,920
Mr. Yamada.

28
00:02:34,920 --> 00:02:36,800
Working part-time, are you?

29
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,680
Well, I'm rather embarrassed to say,

30
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,960
but I've been laid off.

31
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:43,360
So until I find my next job, you see,

32
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:47,120
Please, go ahead.

33
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:50,220
So you knew him, Chief?

34
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:51,760
It was quite a shock.

35
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,980
If I recall, he's about my age.

36
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:57,560
They say it's tough for
middle-aged people to find new jobs.

37
00:02:58,660 --> 00:03:01,640
At least he isn't depressed.
That's the only relief.

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:04,260
You should be careful too, Chief.

39
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:06,640
If you got laid off at that age...

40
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:09,440
Finding a new job is a thorny road.

41
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,640
Don't be stupid.

42
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:14,640
Don't lump me in with you,
the nation's number one screwup.

43
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,720
Listen, Ryotsu.

44
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:19,080
You could be laid off any time, you know.

45
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:21,640
I'm fine.

46
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:25,640
Even if that happens,
I can make a living doing anything.

47
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:29,680
After all,
being a cop is just a part-time job for me.

48
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,400
Idiot! Since when is that
something to brag about?

49
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:36,580
Officer, a suspicious guy
sneaked into the building and...

50
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:44,080
The suspect has been identified as
the wanted serial building burglar.

51
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,940
Thank you for your cooperation.

52
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,700
Then let's escort him
to the police box, Chief.

53
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,740
Ryotsu, why do we have to walk
all the way to the police box?

54
00:03:57,740 --> 00:04:01,500
It can't be helped.
You heard that the patrol cars are all out.

55
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:04,240
Shouldn't we wait for
a patrol car after all?

56
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:10,060
No, taking him in ourselves will
look good for our bonus evaluations.

57
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:13,680
Hold on a second, Chief.

58
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,260
What is it? What's wrong?

59
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,260
I need to pee.

60
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:19,000
What? Don't be a child. Hold it in.

61
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,840
No, I can't! I'm going to leak!

62
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,040
I'll go take care of it in the park here.

63
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,420
Ryotsu, wait!

64
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,860
What a hopeless guy.

65
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:33,100
Boss, hurry up, will you?

66
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:37,140
Don't rush. This is your last look
at the outside world for a while.

67
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:39,280
Take in some good air while you can.

68
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:43,600
Boss, in a place like this,
there's no such thing as good air.

69
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:47,360
Right, where was the restroom again?

70
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:51,060
That Ryotsu, honestly...

71
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:54,020
Hey, stop!

72
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,600
Damn it! Wait!

73
00:04:58,460 --> 00:04:59,180
Stop!

74
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,240
Ryotsu!

75
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:06,440
He's there!

76
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,620
What's this?

77
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:11,060
Damn it! If we let him get away here,
there goes our bonus!

78
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:12,620
But oh no, we've blown it!

79
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:38,680
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

80
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:21,980
Aaaaah!

81
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:23,390
Ryo-san is Ryo-san, granted, but...

82
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:26,180
Ohara, ultimately this is your
supervisory responsibility!

83
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:29,680
I'm sorry. I don't know what to say.

84
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,080
No, I don't want to hear anything!

85
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:32,580
You're fired! Fired!

86
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,200
Fired!?

87
00:06:36,464 --> 00:06:42,700
Chief! The time we feared has come.

88
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,780
So the Chief is getting laid off too,
after all?

89
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:46,960
Idiot! You're getting it too!

90
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:49,260
Just as I thought.

91
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:54,640
I never thought I'd be laid off,
of all people.

92
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:58,940
Chief, sighing won't get us anywhere.

93
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:02,040
Now we have to find our
own way to make a living.

94
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,480
A way to make a living?

95
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:08,060
Yes, we have to take any part-time
job we can and earn our living expenses.

96
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:11,960
Right. Ryotsu,
is there any good part-time job?

97
00:07:11,960 --> 00:07:12,460
Well...

98
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,480
Chief, do you have any special skills?

99
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:20,960
Skills? Let's see...
calligraphy, shogi, and kendo...

100
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:27,160
Those don't count. I mean things like a Grade 1 English
proficiency certificate or being able to use computers.

101
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:35,100
Looks like you've got nothing, then. Those things don't help.
But I have 34 years of experience as a police officer.

102
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:41,980
That's no help at all, is it? Then there's my hazardous materials handling license,
and my cooking certification.

103
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:46,660
And my boiler technician qualification and
my flower arranging instructor certificate.

104
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,820
I've also worked as a
carpenter's apprentice.

105
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:51,260
I can dress people in kimono.

106
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,440
I can tell male from female chicks.

107
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:57,720
And I can do a handstand and
eat spaghetti with my nose.

108
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:02,420
So you really can't do
anything at all, Chief.

109
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:07,780
In that case, finding a job at your
age is going to be really tough.

110
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:12,260
Can't you make an exception somehow?

111
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:16,940
I have to protect my own livelihood too,
you know.

112
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:17,900
Please, Ryotsu.

113
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:21,580
I'm weak when a former
boss asks me for something.

114
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:22,780
A former...

115
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,320
Please.

116
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:27,760
I can't very well refuse
my former boss's request.

117
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,060
Former...

118
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:32,240
Well, with me around,
we'll manage somehow, right?

119
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:34,620
Let's look for part-time jobs together.

120
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:37,140
Please, you're my only hope.

121
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:39,200
Leave it to me.

122
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:50,760
Welcome! Would you like fries with that?

123
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,820
That's a bit stiff.

124
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:54,460
Your eyes aren't smiling.

125
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:58,820
Isn't it because you're surrounded
by young people that you feel hostile?

126
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:00,300
That's not true.

127
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,680
What do you mean?

128
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,980
I just can't stand young people.

129
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:07,880
Come on, you know most of
our customers are young people.

130
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,100
Don't get angry, don't sulk,
don't think about anything.

131
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:14,420
Following the manual is the basics,
after all.

132
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,680
Can you do it?

133
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:17,240
Don't worry, I can.

134
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:20,900
See, you're at it again. This isn't some stubborn old man's shop,
you know.

135
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:22,460
Hey, the order.

136
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:23,960
Yes, coming right up.

137
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:27,680
Welcome!
We have an easy-to-read menu right here.

138
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:31,160
I don't need that.
Just a shake and a cheeseburger will do.

139
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:34,400
Yes, one shake and one cheeseburger,
correct?

140
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:36,800
Would you like fries with that?

141
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:39,360
I said I don't want them. Hurry up already.

142
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:42,580
Yes, one shake, one cheeseburger, please.

143
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:45,340
That'll be 380 yen.

144
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:48,160
Ryotsu's not getting mad? That's a first.

145
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:49,580
Perfect service.

146
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:52,940
Thank you very much, please enjoy your meal.

147
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,760
You held it together well.

148
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:57,560
In fast food, a smile is everything.

149
00:09:57,560 --> 00:10:00,480
Normally I'd kick a guy like that,

150
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:01,700
but it's for the money.

151
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:04,540
Your willingness to do it just
for the money is impressive.

152
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,260
It's for survival.

153
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,380
Welcome, what can I get for you?

154
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:12,540
Come on, Chief, you try it now.

155
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:15,960
Chief, smile, smile!

156
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,300
Welcome, what can I get for you?

157
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:20,200
We have an easy-to-read menu right here.

158
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,580
Why does it have to be an old guy?

159
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:24,540
Seeing old guys makes me angry.

160
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:26,980
What -

161
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:29,220
Chief, calm down. Don't get angry.

162
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:31,360
What can I get for you?

163
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:31,880
Yeah, yeah.

164
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,660
Ugh, old men generally stink, you know.

165
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:36,300
I feel sick.

166
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:39,120
Pff, n-no, wh-what -

167
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:41,080
Heartless or not, patience, patience.

168
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:43,160
U-um, f-for what?

169
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:46,000
Shut up. You, be quiet.

170
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,420
Y-you, calling me "you"?

171
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,220
Patience, patience, patience.

172
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:51,700
Right, I have to be patient. Smile.

173
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,920
Don't give me that creepy smile.

174
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:58,120
Why don't you hold something cuter,
like a little Gyaro?

175
00:10:58,140 --> 00:11:01,280
Honestly, do none of you even know how
to turn up the corners of your mouth?

176
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:07,580
I'll teach you what manners are, you idiot!

177
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:11,720
Seriously, you got fired in three minutes!

178
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:14,140
Apparently that's the store's new record.

179
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:19,640
It paid 680 yen an hour,
and you only got 34 yen, didn't you?

180
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:20,620
Sorry.

181
00:11:21,140 --> 00:11:23,860
Part-time jobs for people in their
fifties are really hard to come by.

182
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:26,420
Let me try here through my connections.

183
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:30,680
Aspiring manga artists,
rock bands before they break out,

184
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:33,600
and aspiring actors, the kind who are said
to all pass through here at least once.

185
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,200
This convenience store part-time job

186
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:37,100
is the job I finally
managed to get for you, so...

187
00:11:37,100 --> 00:11:39,740
This time,
please follow the manual to the letter.

188
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:40,860
Got it.

189
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:44,020
Okay? Listen up.

190
00:11:44,020 --> 00:11:46,520
No matter what kind of customer comes in,
you can't get angry, got it?

191
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:47,660
F-fine, I get it.

192
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:49,200
I'm telling you, there's none.

193
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:50,040
None, none.

194
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:50,760
Welcome!

195
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,341
Wh-, wh-

196
00:11:55,391 --> 00:11:58,080
Wh-, wh-, wh-

197
00:11:59,040 --> 00:11:59,880
It's hot!

198
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,560
Here you go.

199
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:08,880
Damn, this is good!

200
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:15,080
You lot!

201
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:19,560
Do you think you can just help yourselves
to the store's food and drinks?!

202
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:20,560
What?

203
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,180
Shut up, shut up!

204
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:23,620
I'm hungry, damn it!

205
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:25,600
I'll just pay when I leave, all right?

206
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,380
Shoo, shoo, shoo!

207
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,540
You bunch of idiots.

208
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:32,560
And you're no better.

209
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:35,580
Pretending not to see it?
Are you even a man?

210
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:36,840
What's your problem, old man?

211
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:37,700
Listen.

212
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:39,980
Public morals are something

213
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:41,460
You get angry so easily.

214
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:44,220
I'm getting fired again,
aren't I, at this rate.

215
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:57,940
So I really am getting fired after all.

216
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:01,520
What's wrong with the young people in this country,
honestly?

217
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:03,440
There's no use lamenting it, you know.

218
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:06,260
Chief, you're not cut out
for customer-facing work.

219
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:07,020
Yeah.

220
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:10,300
That's why I found something
that's perfect for you, Chief.

221
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:14,240
It pays daily,
and you really feel like you're working.

222
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:17,660
How about it, Chief?

223
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:19,980
You won't have to put on
airs with this one, right?

224
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:21,660
Well, I suppose so.

225
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:28,540
What are you doing, old man?
You're so clumsy.

226
00:13:28,940 --> 00:13:30,160
S-sorry.

227
00:13:30,160 --> 00:13:33,340
Hurry up and finish that, then carry
the building materials over there.

228
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:34,360
Y-yes.

229
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:37,780
Chief, watch your footing carefully.

230
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:41,960
I'm not okay.

231
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,500
I'm taking a little break.

232
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,600
Again?

233
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,140
Well, it can't be helped.

234
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:48,260
Then let's set it down here.

235
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,260
Be careful.

236
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:58,220
Lunch for free, lucky us!

237
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:00,100
Saved!

238
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,840
Chief, at this rate,
after only half a day...

239
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,400
you won't last a single day.

240
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:09,480
Wasn't my lunchbox there?

241
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,380
I left mine there too.

242
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:27,320
You're putting up flyers here?

243
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:29,760
No way, this is illegal!

244
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,740
But Chief keeps getting fired

245
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:32,660
one after another, so...

246
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:34,780
I said no, and that means no!

247
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:36,240
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

248
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:38,220
It's forbidden!

249
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:38,860
Hey!

250
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:40,880
Come with me to the police box for a moment.

251
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,060
No, well

252
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:43,380
No, no, it's not like that.

253
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:45,460
We're from the neighborhood association,

254
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:46,620
we weren't posting those up,

255
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:48,140
we were collecting them.

256
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:49,100
Collecting?

257
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:50,600
Chief, run!

258
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:51,380
Run!

259
00:14:51,620 --> 00:14:52,660
Get in the car, quick!

260
00:14:54,140 --> 00:14:56,140
Chief, hurry and start the car!

261
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:57,340
Sorry!

262
00:14:58,940 --> 00:14:59,900
Yaaah!

263
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:00,480
Run!

264
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:01,320
Everyone, look at this!

265
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:03,960
I can't take this life anymore.

266
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:09,437
Huff, huff.

267
00:15:09,487 --> 00:15:13,680
I never imagined part-time
work would be this hard.

268
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:16,008
That was a good bath.

269
00:15:16,058 --> 00:15:18,220
I've finally shaken off the fatigue.

270
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:20,420
Thank you for your hard work today.

271
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:21,240
Mm.

272
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:26,810
Dear, you've seemed tired lately,

273
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:29,100
so please don't push yourself too hard.

274
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:29,760
Mm.

275
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:34,680
If you, the pillar of this household,
fell ill, it would be a disaster.

276
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,520
Yeah, yeah, mm.

277
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,240
Went pretty well

278
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,400
Went pretty well

279
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,180
Went pretty well

280
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:06,560
Went pretty well

281
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,040
Didn't go so well, did it?

282
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:16,820
This time, no matter what,
you have to tough it out, okay?

283
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:20,300
Since you're my former boss,
I'm going this far for you.

284
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:22,700
Former

285
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,760
This really is the last part-time job,
you hear?

286
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,860
What a height!

287
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:31,820
Don't look down, okay?

288
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:34,120
Make sure you wipe the windows properly.

289
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:36,800
No way, I'm scared, it's way too scary.

290
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:37,820
It's for survival.

291
00:16:37,820 --> 00:16:39,200
I said no, and I mean no!

292
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:41,760
Step away from there!

293
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:42,220
No way!

294
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:43,800
Don't throw a tantrum!

295
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:44,320
Stop it!

296
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:46,020
Whoa! That hurts!

297
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:46,820
Urgh!

298
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:49,720
Urgh! Don't push me here, of all places!

299
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:50,300
Urgh!

300
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:50,960
Whoa!

301
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:51,720
Whoa!

302
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:58,280
Whoa!

303
00:16:59,280 --> 00:16:59,940
One minute!

304
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:10,340
Ryotsu, stop!

305
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:13,940
Down, down!

306
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:14,640
Down?

307
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,420
You went too far, up, up!

308
00:17:21,740 --> 00:17:23,000
Geez, what now?

309
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,440
Stop!

310
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:29,400
Okay, here, lower it slowly.

311
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:31,380
Stop!

312
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,200
Ryotsu, look!

313
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:33,880
What is it?

314
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:37,520
Look, it's him, that Biru Arashi
we let get away the other day!

315
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,140
That bastard!

316
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,560
What do we do, Ryotsu?

317
00:17:48,220 --> 00:17:49,780
Let's kick the window in and go.

318
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:55,680
You idiot! Windows this high up
are all thick and double-glazed!

319
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:58,200
Even if you hit them with a hammer,
you'll only get a crack.

320
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:02,160
And if glass shards fell down,
it would be a disaster.

321
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:06,140
For now, let's climb up first
and go in from the inside.

322
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:07,160
Got it.

323
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:19,660
Right.

324
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:33,740
Chief, hurry up!

325
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:39,680
What floor was it again, Chief?

326
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:44,540
This is the 80th floor,
so it should be about 30 floors down.

327
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:46,840
Alright, for now it's the 50th floor.

328
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:47,600
Roger.

329
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:51,700
Still, it's a relief that today's Sunday.

330
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:54,860
With nobody around,
it'll be easier to spot the culprit.

331
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,740
Ryo-tsu, you go that way.

332
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:00,600
Roger.

333
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:02,740
Wrong.

334
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:04,800
Wrong.

335
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:06,340
Not this one.

336
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:07,680
Wrong.

337
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:09,840
This one's wrong too.

338
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:11,440
Wrong.

339
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:12,900
Wrong.

340
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:13,360
Wrong.

341
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:16,840
Is he there?

342
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,080
Not on this floor.

343
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,620
Right, let's go down one more.

344
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:24,162
Hey,

345
00:19:24,212 --> 00:19:30,420
Are all the rooms on this floor offices?

346
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,300
Yeah.

347
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:34,160
What about private rooms, like a
medicine room or the president's office?

348
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:37,580
Private rooms? If I remember right,
they're two or three floors down.

349
00:19:37,580 --> 00:19:38,080
Right.

350
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,780
Chief, it's two or three floors down.

351
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:46,480
Chief, hurry up. I'm going ahead.

352
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:48,020
Come after me.

353
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:32,440
Wait!

354
00:20:34,380 --> 00:20:35,660
Damn it!

355
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:37,760
Get back here!

356
00:20:40,140 --> 00:20:41,600
Chief, are you all right?

357
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:44,660
I'm fine. He's below us, go!

358
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:45,300
Roger!

359
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:54,780
Damn, he went down!

360
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:04,740
Got him, we've caught up!

361
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,520
Crap, he got off already?

362
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:14,840
Wait, is he really down there?

363
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:37,260
You're not getting away! Prepare yourself!

364
00:21:37,260 --> 00:21:42,460
Wait!

365
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:45,120
Stop!

366
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:53,040
Eeeeeeeh!

367
00:21:57,220 --> 00:21:58,420
Eeeeeeeh!

368
00:21:58,420 --> 00:21:59,420
Eeeeeeeh!

369
00:21:59,420 --> 00:21:59,660
Eeeeeeeh!

370
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:00,080
Eeeeeeeh!

371
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:00,800
Eeeeeeeh!

372
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:01,000
Eeeeeeeh!

373
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Eeeeeeee!

374
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:02,180
Eeeeeeee!

375
00:22:02,180 --> 00:22:02,380
Eeeeeeee!

376
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:02,960
Eeeeeeee!

377
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:03,680
Eeeeeeee!

378
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:03,740
Eeeeeeee!

379
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:04,420
Yes, Chief!

380
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:08,000
Thank you for helping us catch the criminal,

381
00:22:08,820 --> 00:22:10,320
you're the one from that time,

382
00:22:10,980 --> 00:22:11,580
Get out of the way!

383
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,620
Yes, sorry!

384
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:25,120
Ohara, well done! Well done!

385
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:30,560
Even while working a part-time job during your ban period, you were still chasing the criminal.
That's impressive.

386
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:33,340
Well, how should I put it...

387
00:22:33,740 --> 00:22:38,540
I suppose your years of habit as a police
officer led to catching the criminal.

388
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:40,880
Chief, what did you just say?

389
00:22:40,880 --> 00:22:42,420
Ban period.

390
00:22:42,420 --> 00:22:46,620
That's right. Congratulations!
Report back to the field starting tomorrow.

391
00:22:46,620 --> 00:22:48,740
So... I'm fired?

392
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:50,960
Who said anything about firing you?

393
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:55,360
We're not letting go of
outstanding officers like you.

394
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:57,500
Thank you very much.

395
00:22:59,420 --> 00:23:00,980
Glad it worked out, Chief.

396
00:23:00,980 --> 00:23:04,520
Let's both keep doing our best
as police officers together.

397
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:05,800
Ryotsu.

398
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:08,780
Is that right?

399
00:23:09,420 --> 00:23:13,220
That's when I realized being a police
officer was the career change I needed.

400
00:23:13,220 --> 00:23:15,520
I'm glad I became a police officer.

401
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:19,020
So that's why you didn't
show up at the police box.

402
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:20,880
Both Ryo-chan and the Chief,

403
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:26,520
So the Chief's dislike of young
people has eased a bit, right?

404
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:27,620
Yeah, I suppose so.

405
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:30,420
I need to try to understand
their way of thinking too.

406
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:33,620
It's not like I always turn a blind eye.

407
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:36,100
When push comes to shove,
they're pretty capable.

408
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:40,000
Looks aside,
they're surprisingly earnest at heart.

409
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:43,540
You two,

410
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:47,520
you have to throw your magazines in the trash bin properly,
you know!

411
00:23:52,020 --> 00:23:57,420
Young people these days are hopeless,
they always have been!

412
00:24:01,220 --> 00:24:05,660
Kick the alarm clock away my little toe!

413
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:14,020
Draw on my eyebrows real quick,
then dash, dash, dash to the station!

414
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:19,660
Packed train,
dozing off on some old man's back.

415
00:24:20,740 --> 00:24:25,960
Another tough week, and the
unreasonable demands are fair enough.

416
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:33,300
But I'm getting by one-handed, with a
beef bowl, extra sauce, and a cloudy day.

417
00:24:33,900 --> 00:24:40,340
Endless overtime frustration,
cleared right up with more frustration!

418
00:24:43,700 --> 00:24:50,120
Every day is no-problem-blend,
once I've rinsed off in a hot shower.

419
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:56,720
Every day, no-problem-brain!
Recharging with my sleep pillow.

420
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:06,340
Every day, no-problem-brain!
I love this me just as I am.

421
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:13,140
Every day, no-problem-brain!
Hearts flying on a Monday.

422
00:25:13,140 --> 00:25:17,200
Antec, Antec, no-problem-brain!

423
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:22,640
A profiler from headquarters?

424
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:28,920
Profiling is the latest investigative method,
where you analyze the criminal's psychology to work out how many culprits there are.

425
00:25:29,340 --> 00:25:33,060
I get that,
but why do we have to dress up like this?

426
00:25:33,460 --> 00:25:37,140
Next time,
be a shoujo manga detective, got it?

427
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:50,860
Thank you.

